              "pages": {
                "end": 48,
                "start": 48
              }
            }
          ],
          "text": "Petitioners argue that the presumption should be limited to patent cases, not copyright cases, and that the burden of proof should shift to the defendant."
        },
        {
          "attribution": "Petitioners",
          "citations": [
            {
              "document_hash": "a3641987d8fd0d06335e722ab03fbfae3d2449c626a3ff8c33d0a9321dfc8f12",
              "evidence_ids": [
                "ev-a3641987d8fd-0002-0001"
              ],
              "pages": {
                "end": 54,
                "start": 54
              }
            }
          ],
          "text": "Petitioners contend that the presumption makes sense regardless of the size of the patentee because the patentee has better information about the market for the tying product."
        },
        {
          "attribution": "Ms. Sullivan",
          "citations": [
            {
              "document_hash": "a3641987d8fd0d06335e722ab03fbfae3d2449c626a3ff8c33d0a9321dfc8f12",
              "evidence_ids": [
                "ev-a3641987d8fd-0003-0000"
              ],
              "pages": {
                "end": 55,
                "start": 55
              }
            }
          ],
          "text": "According to Ms. Sullivan, ms. Sullivan, speaking for the petitioners, describes the presumption as narrow, rebuttable, and fair to shift the burden to the defendant."
        }
